# This file contains the Ukrainian localization of the
# Raku Programming Language.
#
# CONTRIBUTORS:
#
# Andrew Shitov
#
# This file is the source the two modules are generated FROM.  After
# changing anything below, regenerate them from the distribution root with
#
#     rakudo regen
#
# which is `update-localization` from the L10N distribution plus the handling
# of `|`-separated spellings.  A translation naming several of them,
#
#     scope-my  мій|моя|мої|моє
#
# means the slang accepts every one and the deparser prints the first.  Only
# the first reaches the grammar by default, because Raku++ cannot match an
# alternation inside a slang token; `rakudo regen --synonyms` turns the rest
# on for Rakudo.
#
# Either way it needs Rakudo: Raku++ runs the modules generated here
# but cannot load L10N itself, stopping at `use L10N` with "the module
# registered no slang".
#
# See https://github.com/Raku-L10N/L10N/ for the localization framework.

